<title>USA: Daschle sees U.S. ethanol subsidy being extended.</title>
<headline>Daschle sees U.S. ethanol subsidy being extended.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senate Democratic Leader Tom Daschle said Thursday he believed the ethanol subsidy would be extended through 2007.</p>
<p>The Senate has 60 bipartisan votes in favor of extending the subsidy, the South Dakota Democrat said.  &quot;It will be extended to the year 2007,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The House tax bill would allow the subsidy to expire at the end of 2000, while the Senate tax bill would cut the subsidy in later years.  Senate Majority Leader Trent Lott, a Mississippi Republican, earlier said &quot;I presume the ethanol program will be continued.&quot;</p>
</text>
